## Ticket Information

| | |
| --- | --- |
| **Ticket #** | GL-1042 |
| **Ticket Name** | Payee Management \| bulk payee creation and editing via command line tool \| Payee State — Pending |

**User Story**

> As a manager for a program on GridLens, I want any payees created or edited via the bulk
> payee command line tool to automatically be placed in a Pending state, so that they follow
> the same payee approval workflow as payees created and edited through the GridLens UI, and
> no bulk-created or bulk-edited payee can receive a payment or be propagated to Ledgerline
> without first being reviewed and approved by Finance.

**Description**

The ticket aligns bulk payee creation and editing performed through the command management
script with the Payee Approval Workflow. Bulk-created and bulk-edited payees must enter the
Pending state, and Ledgerline Organization API propagation must be deferred until Finance
approval. Duplicate Ledgerline Organization Code validation must continue during bulk
creation, and audit/change log tracking must be maintained.

**Business Impacts**

- Prevents unapproved payees from being propagated to Ledgerline.
- Enforces a consistent approval workflow regardless of creation or edit method.
- Protects data integrity through duplicate Ledgerline Organization Code validation.
- Maintains auditability through required change log entries.

**Impacted Roles**

- Program Managers (per user story)
- GridLens Support Users running bulk scripts
- Finance Approver Users reviewing payees

## Acceptance Criteria

| AC ID | Acceptance Criteria |
| --- | --- |
| **AC-1** | All payees created via the bulk command management script are automatically set to Pending state upon creation. No bulk-created payee defaults to Approved. Pending state behaves identically to UI-created payees. |
| **AC-2** | All payees edited via the bulk command management script are automatically moved to Pending state upon edit submission. Previously Approved payees must return to Pending until re-approved. |
| **AC-3** | No Ledgerline Organization records are created or updated during bulk create/edit; API calls are deferred until approval. Duplicate Ledgerline Organization Code validation still occurs during bulk creation, and failures are clearly identified. |
| **AC-4** | Bulk-created and bulk-edited payees appear in the Payee List View with Pending state displayed. |
| **AC-5** | Bulk-created payees generate a change log entry with Date, By, Action = Payee Created, and required Note. |
| **AC-6** | Bulk-edited payees generate a change log entry with Date, By, Action = Payee Edited, and required Note. |

